  "body": "## What\n\n`session/selectModel` now applies to a session that has already started, matching DSH's own contract (the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller` resolves the model and applies it to the next request). Before this change the Web host answered `session/model-frozen` for any draft that had admitted input, so the model picker in the composer looked alive but every switch after the first message failed with `模型操作失败：session/model-frozen: Model selection can change only before this Web draft has any admitted input, tool activity, attachment, or child session`.\n\n## Why\n\n`EFFECTIVE_AGENT_SNAPSHOT_KEY` is the only place `prepareTurn -> resolveAgent` reads the model from, so re-freezing that snapshot is the whole switch - no wider config widening, no drift-bypass. `checkSessionConfigDrift` keeps its baseline because the alias row keeps the selection it was created with.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `packages/core/src/runtime/runtime.ts`: additive `setSessionModel(sessionId, model)` re-freezes the effective-agent model and the session row. Fails closed on a missing, corrupt, or foreign snapshot, and rejects an empty reference.\n- `packages/contracts/src/message.ts` + `packages/core/src/runtime/model-call-controller.ts`: assistant messages record the model that produced them.\n- `apps/web/src/deepseek/projections.ts`: `modelSelection.lastUsed` follows the settled journal (per-message provenance) instead of the mutable session row, and no longer rewrites history that a client already holds. Without this the follow stream correctly refused the changed prefix (`历史加载失败：Durable projection prefix changed during follow`).\n- `apps/web/src/deepseek/routes.ts` (new): route-aware provider. A switched model is served lazily through the route that owns it while the owner's `getConfigIdentity()` stays exactly as created, so frozen fingerprints are untouched.\n- `apps/web/src/deepseek/owners.ts`: a started draft switches in place; a pristine draft keeps the existing frozen-replacement path and its tests.\n- `apps/web/src/main.ts`: base provider is wrapped route-aware so the base harness can switch too.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm typecheck` (`tsc -b`) exit 0.\n- Target suites: `apps/web/src/deepseek/{owners,composition.integration,projections,activity,catalog,session-model-snapshot}.test.ts` + `packages/core/src/runtime/effective-config.test.ts` = 101 passed.\n- Broader run (`apps/web packages/core packages/harness`): 1584 passed, 5 failed - 3 are the pre-existing Windows symlink cases (`EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink`; this host has no developer mode), 2 are `apps/web/src/harness.integration.test.ts` timing flakes that pass 6/6 when that file runs alone.\n- Live 8787 run (real browser, real upstream through cli-proxy-api at 127.0.0.1:8317): create a provider reference `probe` -> select `probe/deepseek-flash` -> send \"只回复两个字：好的\" -> answered \"好的\" in 10s -> switch to `probe/glm-5.3-flash` (HTTP 200, no toast, trigger label updates, history still rendered) -> send \"只回复两个字：收到\" -> answered \"收到\" in 13s, footer `2 轮 2 步`. Upstream log shows both `POST /v1/chat/completions` 200s.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- The owner's context budget still reflects the model that created the owner; the budget is not re-derived per turn (frozen per P27-4).\n- Legacy sessions with no frozen effective-agent snapshot still refuse with `Legacy sessions keep their frozen model` - there is no frozen model to switch.\n- The routed client falls back to the owner's own route when a model cannot be resolved, so a foreign model id is never sent to the wrong upstream.",
